{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"uncovered-sonic-nightheron","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n\n`sweep (macos, full suite)` fails on `main` at `6b034b9f8224`, reddening the branch-head run\n(`33846424069`). Unlike `sweep (windows)`, this job has **no `continue-on-error`**\n(`.github/workflows/test.yml:370-373`), so it does affect the run conclusion — **main is red because\nof it.**\n\n```\n==================================== ERRORS ====================================\n_ ERROR at teardown of test_provisioning_installs_then_builds_and_leaves_the_bundle...\n[gw0] darwin -- Python 3.13.14\n19243 passed, 72 skipped, 422 warnings, 1 error in 2687.89s (0:44:47)\n```\n\nAll four `build-and-test / pytest` matrix cells pass, including `macos-latest, py3.13`. Only the\n**full-suite** macOS sweep fails, and only in **teardown**.\n\n## This is a regression introduced by change 2600\n\n`tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py` was added by `668523feffde` (change 2600, bug\n`9a17-e0b3-7aa6-4091`). Before that commit the job passed: `sweep (macos, full suite)` = success in\nruns `33725525516`, `33757757270`, `33792688019` and `33824556786`.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe error is in the **autouse** `_no_repo_commits` guard at `tests/conftest.py:774`, whose purpose is\nto fail any test that moves the checkout's HEAD:\n\n```\n    before = _repo_head(_REPO_ROOT)\n    yield\n    if before is None:\n        return\n>   after = _repo_head(_REPO_ROOT)\ntests/conftest.py:774\ntests/_isolation.py:68: in head\n    return _run_git_probe(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").stdout.strip()\ntests/_isolation.py:39: in _run_git_probe\n    return _run_process(\n.../subprocess.py: stdout, stderr = process.communicate(input, timeout=timeout)\n```\n\nSo the guard's post-test `git rev-parse HEAD` probe fails or times out **after** this test. The test\nitself passes; only its teardown errors.\n\nThe likely cause is resource contention rather than a git problem: this test provisions a **real**\nNode toolchain (`npm ci` plus an esbuild bundle) and is the heaviest thing in the suite. On the\nmacOS runner, in a 45-minute full-suite run under xdist, the guard's short-timeout subprocess probe\nappears not to complete. **Verify this rather than assume it** — an alternative reading is that\nprovisioning leaves a child process or open handle that interferes with the probe, which would be a\ndifferent and more serious defect.\n\n## Why it did not show up pre-merge\n\nThe Verified lane's macOS job runs only the `platform_compat` marker selection\n(`DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS`), not the full suite — the full macOS suite is schedule-only. So the patchset\nlane structurally could not have caught this, exactly as `sweep (windows)` and the\n`scanner-integration` job were structurally not exercised on the changes that introduced them. That\nis the fourth instance of this shape in one day and the ticket should not treat it as incidental.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nDeterministic, verifiable in one run — no \"run it again and see\".\n\n1. The cause is **established, not assumed**: determine whether the probe times out under load, or\n   whether provisioning leaves a process/handle that breaks it. Quote the evidence. The two have\n   different fixes and guessing between them is how this recurs.\n2. `sweep (macos, full suite)` passes on `main`. Because the job is schedule/dispatch-gated, verify\n   by `workflow_dispatch` of `test.yml` against the fix, not by waiting ~6 hours for the schedule.\n3. The fix does not weaken the `_no_repo_commits` guard's protection. That guard exists to catch a\n   test committing into the checkout, and it has already earned its keep tonight. If the fix touches\n   the guard rather than the test, a test must fail if the guard stops detecting a real HEAD move.\n4. If the cause is provisioning cost, the fix must not simply skip the test on macOS — that would be\n   the \"absence of execution reported as success\" pattern this repo has hit four times today. Either\n   make it affordable, or mark it explicitly and loudly as not-run-on-macOS with a recorded reason.\n5. Defect-seeded: demonstrate the failure reproducing before the fix (a forced-contention or\n   forced-timeout reproduction is acceptable and preferable to a 45-minute run), then passing after.\n\n## File impact\n\n`tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py`, and possibly `tests/conftest.py` / `tests/_isolation.py`\nif the probe's timeout or robustness is the correct place to fix it.","id":"860b-28eb-10c0-4249","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["bug","ci","macos","e2e","regression"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"sweep (macos, full suite) fails on main: teardown git-HEAD probe errors after the e2e toolchain provisioning test added by 2600"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788509806917390001,"uuid":"ffaac0e1-249a-48f1-bef3-68cf80a506ba"}